A||||9||Fformula88||Best way to add 3-spoke wheel to Formula||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||06-06-2001||05:04 PM||||I want to add a leather 3-spoke wheel to my Formula, but have run across a problem.  I've been thinking of getting Fierostore's wheel, but its not going to work as is.  After talking to them, they think I will need the hub off of an existing 3 spoke wheel for the horn wiring.  I will also need the center cap/button for the horn.  <P>My question is can the hubs be interchanged?  I was looking at the one on my dads SE, and it doesn't look like it comes apart.  I didn't take it off the column either, so I may have missed something.  Anybody who has had any experience with them, can the swap be done?  Should I get a used wheel out of a junked car for the hub?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||06-06-2001||05:57 PM||||I put a used GT wheel on my Formula. You should not have to change the whole hub. I had to get the horn "springy thingy" off of an 84 parts car I had. The horn works fine. I believe the center cap/button off of it would fit also but my wheel came with the GT one so I used it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||06-06-2001||06:03 PM||||To try to clarify:<P>OK the "springy thingy" is a little plastic clip with a spring in it that pushes down thru the wheel into the hub and twist locks in place to make the horn work. On the Formula it has a wire coming out of it that goes to the paddle buttons. On the GT and 84 (others with center horn button???) it is made the same where it goes thru the wheel/hub but just has a steel piece to make contact with the center cap instead of the wire.||||reg||1
Z||000003||cadaver||06-06-2001||06:03 PM||||They are all the same. If you go from a four spoke to a three then yes you need the little spring thing. But they all bolt on. I have a wheel from some other kind of pontiac. A grand am maybe. And that bolted on. I probably have a spring thing if you need.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex2004||06-06-2001||06:43 PM||||So are all Fiero steering wheel's interchangable?  I have a 3 spoke on my 84 which is slightly bent and i cannot turn the bright lights on unless i turn the steering wheel and i was wanting to put a 4 spoke steering wheel from like an 86 +. If so, is it very hard to change them out? <P>Alex..||||reg||5
Z||000005||theogre||06-06-2001||07:37 PM||||All OE Fiero steering wheels should be the same as far as mounting to the column. They are held by one nut and you need a wheel puller. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fformula88||06-06-2001||09:01 PM||||Thanks for all your responses.  I guess I am just confused as to what the problem with this "new" wheel would be.  By the pictures online, the wheel does not appear to have the center stuff in it (to clarify, it appears to have nothing where the nut goes to hold the wheel onto the column).  <P>I figured they would be fairly interchangeable.  GM likes to keep it all simple.  I've got the wheel puller too.  Just have to find a good wheel!  Thanks again everyone!||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||06-07-2001||12:14 AM||||OK, I see why you were asking now. I never noticed the GT wheel would come apart before. The Formula one sure won't. I did confirm that a plain 84 horn button will fit a GT wheel. Color was off a bit, more a  dark gray where the GT is more black... don't know if that's all of them or if the one I have is faded. <P>Maybe the inside part of an 84 might fit as well??? If so, they are a lot easier to find and cheaper.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000008||Phil||06-07-2001||09:28 AM||||Formula wheels come apart. The rectangular center section pops right off.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fformula88||06-07-2001||02:32 PM||||I decided to order one of the wheels to see what its got with it.  After it arrives, I'll figure out what else it needs to make everything work.  I know I am going to need the center cap/horn button.  There are a few junked Fieros around here so I should be able to get that without problem.  ||||reg||1
